   "id": "math.derivative-at-point",
   "name": "Derivative at a point",
   "requires": [],
   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "The derivative f′(a) is the gradient of the tangent to y = f(x) at (a, f(a)). It is what (f(a + h) − f(a))/h approaches as h gets closer to 0 from both sides. If it exists, f is differentiable at a."
    },
    "am": {
     "text": "f′(a) በ (a, f(a)) ላይ ያለው የታንጀንቱ ግራዲየንት ነው፤ h ከሁለቱም አቅጣጫ ወደ 0 ሲቀርብ (f(a + h) − f(a))/h የሚቀርበው ቁጥር።",
     "machine": true
    }
   },
